== General ==

<div class="mp-section collapsible collapsed">
<h3 class="mp-title" style="display: block; position: relative">[[File:Ore UI - "Crafting Table Block" Icon.png|40px|left|class=pixel-image]] General</h3>
''A bunch of stuff, from network settings to game credits''
<div class="collapsible-content">
----
==== Network settings ====
''Adjust the online experience on a technical and social level''
----
; Allow mobile data for online play [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Use Mobile data for Multiplayer when Wi-Fi is unavailable. This might incur additional data costs''
: Toggles to allow [[multiplayer]] connections when connected to a mobile network instead of Wi-Fi. When joining an online game with mobile data, an icon is shown on the [[loading screen]]. Only available for mobile devices, cannot be changed in-game.
----
; Enable WebSockets [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Connect to a WebSockets server for the setup of external scripts and other automated features''
----
; Require Encrypted Websockets [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button Locked (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Securely encrypt data between WebSockets and Minecraft''
: Only allows WebSocket connections with encryption. Locked when "Websockets Enabled" is disabled.
----
; Automatically update content packs <div class="tright">Windows, console: [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]<br><br>'''Mobile:<div style="font-family:Minecraft">On with Wi-Fi only</div></div>
''Newly released versions of your packs will be downloaded as soon as they're available''
: Downloaded [[Marketplace]] packs are automatically updated when an update is available and the player is in the menus. On mobile, there are three available options, offering to only download updates with a Wi-Fi connection or allow downloading using cellular data.
----
; Tutorial<ref name="tutorial">Not available for certain players, {{cite bug|MCPE|184669|Tutorial option does not appear sometimes}}</ref> [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Get in-game tips to learn the basics of Minecraft''
: Toggles the [[tutorial hints]] when playing the first few times in a world. Only available for certain players.
----
; ''Restart Tutorial''<ref name="tutorial" /> <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Restart</div>
''Restarts the tutorial in case you missed something''
: Resets all tutorial hints and shows all toasts again when playing in a world, when the tutorial has been finished before. Only available for certain players.
----
; Only allow trusted skins [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
: Toggle to replace custom imported [[skins]] of other players with default skins.
----
; Filter profanity [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Filter out inappropriate language''
: Toggles the Xbox profanity filter for all player-created text in-game (such as [[chat]]s), replacing inappropriate language with hashes (#). This can only be disabled if the account received confirmation from the Xbox privacy settings.
----
; Enable Game Pause [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''A single-player feature that pauses gameplay while the game menu is open''
: Pauses the game while in the [[pause menu]] in [[singleplayer]]. This option is only available in-game.
----
; Show Pause Menu on Focus Lost [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Shows the pause menu when switching to another application''
: Opens the pause menu when the application loses focus, available on Windows only.
----

==== Miscellaneous ====
''We didn't know where else to put these settings''
----
; Lower framerate when controller is disconnected [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
: Shows a pop-up on the screen and drastically lowers the FPS the connection to the controller gets lost, if in controller mode. Cannot be toggled in-game.
----
; ''Help Center'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Open</div>
''Get answers to all of your burning support queries''
: Opens the [https://help.minecraft.net/hc/en-us Minecraft Help Center].
----
; ''Credits'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">View</div>
''All the people who helped make this game''
: Opens the [[credits]] sequence.
----
; ''Attribution'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">View</div>
''Technology partners and systems''
: Opens the [https://minecraft.net/en-us/attribution/ attribution] site.
----
; ''Licensed content'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Open</div>
''All licensed content available in Minecraft''
: Opens the [https://minecraft.net/en-us/licensed-content/ licensed content] site.
----
; ''Font license'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Open</div>
''A license for third-party fonts''
: Shows the [[Noto Sans]] font license in a pop-up.
----
; ''Tinkering list'' <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Open</div>
''Technical info that's not relevant for players. Feel free to have a look if you're curious!''
: Opens a tinkering list in a pop-up. This contains random item names, some of which do not exist, with unknown purpose (Glass Bottle, Blue Base Sinister Canton, etc.).
