<div class="mp-section collapsible collapsed">
<h5 class="mp-title" style="display: block; position: relative">Ray Traced</h5>
<div class="collapsible-content">
----
; Brightness <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">50%</div>
''If your screen is still too dark, change the settings on your device, TV, or monitor''
: Adjusts the brightness of the game. Dims down or lights up the game's surfaces, even if fully dark. It has no effect on gameplay, it is a visual effect. Works in any dimension and affects the [[Night Vision]] status effect.
----
; Framerate Limit <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Unlimited</div>
''Set a limit for maximum frames per second to keep a steady frame rate or prevent overheating your device''
: Limits how many frames the game can render per second. Slider can be set between 30 and 60 FPS with steps of 5, or Unlimited.
----
; Anti-Aliasing <div class="tright"><span style="font-family:Minecraft">2</span><ref name="varies" group="note">Default on most Windows devices, varies depending on the device specifications.</ref></div>
''Not a trick question. How smooth do you like your blocks?''
: Adjusts the amount of [[w:Multisample_anti-aliasing|multisample anti aliasing]], which smooths the image and removes jagged edges. Available options are powers of 2 between 1 and 16. Not available on mobile devices.
----
; Upscaling [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
: Significantly boosts frame rates on GeForce RTX graphics cards with NVIDIA DLSS 2.0.
----
; Ray Tracing Render Distance <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">8 chunks</div>
''This high render distance could cause a low frame rate, crashes, or other unexpected behavior''<ref group="note">Only shown if set above recommended value.</ref>
: Controls the distance in which [[chunk]]s are rendered. Slider can be set between 5 and 24 chunks, but can be changed to any value in options.txt, similar to Vibrant Visuals.
----
</div></div>
----
; Render Clouds [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Happy little clouds in the sky''
: Toggles the [[clouds]] graphics, requires "Beatiful Skies" to be enabled.
----
; Fancy Leaves [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Leaves but better''
: Toggles transparent [[leaves]].
----
; Fancy Bubbles [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Bubbles with style''
: Toggles the water [[bubbles]] graphics between particles inside bubble collumns or animated bubble textures on the side of bubble collumns. Not available in-game.
----
; Improved input response [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Makes the game react faster when you press buttons or move. May increase power consumption''
: Reduces delay between inputs and what is displayed on-screen. Grayed out when the graphics mode is set to Vibrant Visuals or Ray Traced, and only available on Windows.
----
; Frame pacing [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Turn this on for a smoother, more stable experience. This may cap your game at a lower frame rate''
: Only available on mobile devices.
----
; UI Profile <div class="tright">Windows, console: <span style="font-family:Minecraft">Classic</span><br>'''Mobile:<span style="font-family:Minecraft"> Pocket</span>'''</div>
''Select Pocket (mobile) or Classic interface layouts''
: Changes the game's [[GUI]] style between classic and Pocket.
----
==== View customization ====
''Build, stream, or take screenshots without distractions''
----
; Camera Perspective <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">First Person</div>
''Select the in-game camera's point of view''
: Toggles camera perspective between regular '''First Person''' and [[third-person view]], '''Third Person Back''' and '''Third Person Front'''. This can also be toggled with {{key|F5}} or {{Xbutton|seriesdpad-up}} by default, or the optional camera perspective button on touchscreen.
----
; Fullscreen [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Minecraft, in full screen''
: Toggles between windowed and fullscreen mode, also toggleable with {{keys|F11}}. Only available on Windows.
----
; Hide Hand [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Hide your hand in first-person view''
: Toggles to hide the player [[hand]] and items, but show any other HUD elements, or vice versa and only show the hand.
----
; Hide Paper Doll [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Hide your character preview when swimming, sneaking, flying, or riding''
: Toggles the side-view of the player displayed in the top-left corner of the screen during special movements, toggleable with {{keys|F8}}.
----
; Hide HUD [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Hide your Heads Up Display, including health, hunger, and item bars''
: Toggles to hide all [[HUD]] elements, but the hand and paper doll can be re-enabled individually. This can also be toggled with {{keys|F1}}.
----
; HUD Opacity <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">100%</div>
''How much you can see-trough the Heads Up Display''
: Changes the opacity of several HUD elements.
----
; Splitscreen HUD Opacity
''{{info needed}}''
: Changes the opacity of the HUD, while in [[splitscreen]] mode. Only available on consoles.
----
; Change Screen Safe Area <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">100.0</div>
''Make sure the game looks great in your device's screen''
: Opens a menu with a slider controlling the offset of the corners of the screen, moving the UI elements further inside. Not available in-game.
----
; Splitscreen <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">Horizontal</div>
''{{info needed}}''
: Toggles between horizontal and vertical orientation of the splitscreen. Only available on consoles.
----
; FOV <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">60°</div>
''Viewing angle of the in-game camera''
: Changes the field of view, which can make the screen appear more zoomed in or out. The actual field of view depends on the aspect ratio of the screen. Available options range from 30° to 110° with steps of 1°.
----
; Field of view can be altered by gameplay [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Allow gameplay effects like sprinting or potion use to temporarily change the Field Of View''
: Toggles whether gameplay, such as speed changes, can change the field of fiew.
----
; Show player names [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Display names above other players' heads''
: Toggles to show nametags from other [[player]]s.
----
; Splitscreen player names [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''{{info needed}}''
: Toggles to show the player names in the corner of each splitscreen section, indicating which screen belongs to which player. Only available on consoles.
----
; Show autosave icon [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Display an icon when the game is autosaving''
: Toggles the [[autosave]] icon in the top-right of the screen.
----
==== Accessibility: Video ====
''Controls to make Minecraft more comfortable to play''
----
; UI scale modifier <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">100%</div>
''Select the size of the HUD and other UI elements to make them easier to use on different devices''
: Adjusts the scale of the all [[menu screen]]s, [[UI]] elements, and [[GUI]]s. Smaller scales are only available on higher resolutions. Available options on 4K displays (max for ''Minecraft'') are '''50%''', '''63%''', '''75%''', '''88%''', and '''100%''', percentages may differ depending on the resolution.
----
; Extra large new UI [[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Increase the size of the UI for clarity and easy reading''
: Enables an extra large version of the [[Ore UI]] menu interface, locking "UI scale modifier" to 100%.
----
; Screen Animations [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Subtle HUD animations to help transition from one screen to another''
: Toggles the animations when switching GUIs or menus, certain UI animations like [[splash]] text bobbing, the animated [[Marketplace]] button, and the [[panorama]] scrolling.
----
; View Bobbing [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Camera bobs when walking''
: Toggles to show the bobbing animation when walking.
----
; Damage Tilt <div class="tright"; style="font-family:Minecraft">100%</div>
''The amount of camera shake caused by being hurt''
: Adjusts how much the screen shakes and changes field of view when taking [[damage]].
----
; Camera Shake [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]
''Set up camera shake using macros or chat''
: Whether the camera can visually shake using {{cmd|camerashake}} or creator features.
----
; Outline Selection <div class="tright">Windows, console: [[File:Ore UI - Toggle ON Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]<br><br>'''Mobile:'''[[File:Ore UI - Toggle OFF Button (Bedrock).png|55px|right|link=]]</div>
''Makes it easier to see which block you're looking at''
: Toggles the outline selection of blocks.
----
</div></div>
